# ============================================================================
# Excluded from the Docker BUILD CONTEXT — never baked into an image layer.
#
# This is a privacy boundary, not just a size optimization. portfolio/holdings.json,
# portfolio/bonds.json and the *_history.json files hold your REAL money — how much
# you own, what you paid, your cost basis. An image layer is a distributable
# artifact: if it ever contains these files, anyone who receives or pulls that
# image (a registry, a teammate, a backup) receives your financial data with it,
# permanently, even if you later delete the file — old layers persist in image
# history. This file is what stops that from being possible in the first place.
#
# At RUNTIME, your real portfolio/ directory is bind-mounted into the running
# container from the host (see docker-compose.yml) — completely different from
# being copied into the image at build time. The app reads it live; the image
# itself never contains it. That is the whole point of this file.
# ============================================================================

# ---- Private financial data — NEVER let these into an image layer ----
portfolio/holdings.json
portfolio/bonds.json
portfolio/history.json
portfolio/bonds_history.json

# ---- Local Python environment ----
venv/
.venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# ---- Generated, regenerated fresh inside the container anyway ----
data/
reports/
logs/

# ---- Secrets — passed as real environment variables at `docker run` /
# `docker compose up` time (see docker-compose.yml's env_file:), never
# copied into the image ----
.env
.env.local
*.env
!.env.example

# ---- VCS / editor / OS cruft ----
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- Claude Code project settings (local paths, not relevant in-image) ----
.claude/

# ---- Docs not needed at runtime (kept out of the image; still in git) ----
CLAUDE.md
